Id: dbs020i
Severity: INFO
Category: services
Check: check_databases
Fix: Rename CONFIG to something unguessable (rename-command CONFIG ...), or to "" to disable it.
References: redis-server(1)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

Redis answers CONFIG under its own name: anyone reaching the
server reads and rewrites its configuration at runtime.
Renaming the command blunts the automated attacks that assume
it; disabling it outright is safest where nothing needs it.
